    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures \u2014 the other test files are the abstract base and its helpers).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field following the existing derived-field pattern used for `membershipNumber`:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getMembershipTier()` getter that returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is `0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `BRONZE`. Null-safe on both fields.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `membershipTier` as a read-only string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field. MapStruct then maps it by name automatically (same mechanism as `membershipNumber`/`namesakeCount`), so it's serialized on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE).",
